/*! \mainpage preC-SUMO Developer Guide

\tableofcontents

\section intro Introduction
preC-SUMO is the coupling-side adapter between D-FlowFM and C-SUMO in a preCICE setup.

Current core responsibilities are:
- read and validate C-SUMO settings,
- register preCICE meshes and data channels,
- receive far-field data from preCICE and write FF2NF input files,
- wait for and read NF2FF output files,
- convert NF2FF results to connected sink/source writes for D-FlowFM via preCICE.

For the underlying preCICE concepts and API details, see the external documentation:
- <a href="https://precice.org/docs.html">preCICE documentation</a>

For the canonical build and example workflow, see \ref build_and_run_example_12.

\section reading_path Recommended Reading Path
For a developer-oriented overview without opening the implementation, read the documentation in this order:
1. this page for the system overview and runtime workflow,
2. \ref build_and_run_example_12 for the concrete example setup and launch scripts,
3. the code entry points below when you want to map the design to implementation files.

\section coupling_workflow Core Coupling
The coupling between D-Flow FM and C-SUMO is handled using preCICE. The D-FlowFM has an adapter implementation which does the conversion between FM mesh/data to and from preCICE. 
The preC-SUMO executable is a wrapper that interacts with preCICE, writes FF2NF files that are consumed by the C-SUMO application, and reads the resulting NF2FF files, which are then sent to FM using preCICE.

Initialize the FM-to-preC-SUMO exchanges, not the exchanges sent by preC-SUMO.
Before preCICE initialization, preC-SUMO waits for and reads the initial NF2FF files, converts their
results to determine the initial sink/source mesh, and registers that mesh. It does not send this
initial conversion as coupling data. Configurations requiring initial data from preC-SUMO are rejected:
NF2FF responses can depend on incoming FM values, especially when converting excess constituents to
absolute values, and those FM values are available only after preCICE initialization.

\dotfile coupled_solvers_fm_csumo.dot "FM and preC-SUMO coupling overview"

\section architecture Architecture Overview
The system-level picture below shows the surrounding coupled components: D-Flow FM, the preCICE adapter,
C-SUMO, and the NF2FF/FF2NF exchange files.
\image html FM-C-SUMO_scheme_precice.drawio.svg "Coupled FM/C-SUMO architecture via preCICE" width=1000px
preCICE offers tools like config-visualizer which can be used to view the in use precice-config file.

\section runtime_workflow Runtime Workflow
The system overview above shows the participating components. The runtime workflow below gives a high-level view of the preC-SUMO processing sequence and interaction points.

FM reads and installs sink/source data at relative time zero immediately after preCICE initialization,
before computing its first interval. This supports partners providing initial forcing without
partner-specific logic. With preC-SUMO return exchanges not initialized, default zero discharge
means no initial coupled water or constituent transfer.

At subsequent coupling boundaries, FM redefines its 3D mesh when permitted, writes its fields,
and advances preCICE before reading and installing the response for the next FM interval.
The response read refreshes the received sink/source mesh size and vertex IDs to account for remeshing.
Reading and installing before the exchange would apply the previous response for an extra interval.

For each preCICE window, preC-SUMO reads the FM fields, writes FF2NF files, waits for the corresponding
NF2FF files, converts the results, writes sink/source data, and advances by the full available window.
With parallel-explicit coupling, preC-SUMO still computes its response using previously exchanged
FM fields. The ordering above avoids an additional application delay; it does not provide
same-boundary FM-to-preC-SUMO-to-FM feedback. Serial coupling with remeshing is tracked in
<a href="https://github.com/precice/precice/issues/2177">precice/precice#2177</a>.

\dotfile preC_SUMO_Core_Workflow.dot "preC-SUMO core workflow overview"

For the preCICE calls alone, including mesh registration and conditional sink/source mesh resets,
see the adapter-only mermaid diagram. File exchange and near-field processing are intentionally omitted.

`docs/include/preC_SUMO_adapter_sequence_diagram.mmd` for viewing in a Mermaid-capable editor.

For a joint FM/preC-SUMO exchange overview, see
`docs/include/FM_preC_SUMO_Exchange_Overview.mmd`.
preC-SUMO has no independent internal timestep or subcycling: each iteration uses
`getMaxTimeStepSize()` and advances by the full available preCICE window.
FM, in contrast, accumulates its user timesteps until the exchange boundary.

For the detailed per-step swimlane view, see \ref pre_c_sumo::run in the API reference.

